Requirements

To run this project, you need:

Java Development Kit 8 or later

Command Prompt, Terminal, or an IDE such as IntelliJ IDEA, Eclipse, or Visual Studio Code

Check your Java installation:

java -version
javac -version

Installation and Execution

Clone the repository:

git clone https://github.com/your-username/adaptive-traffic-signal.git


Navigate to the project directory:

cd adaptive-traffic-signal


Compile the program:

javac Main.java


Run the application:

java Main

Example

Consider the following traffic:

North : 20 vehicles
South : 10 vehicles
East  : 40 vehicles
West  : 10 vehicles


The total number of vehicles is:

20 + 10 + 40 + 10 = 80


Since East has the highest number of vehicles, the adaptive signal selects East.

The green signal duration is then calculated based on the traffic distribution.

